WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.380
Superheroes stick together.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.460
In the aftermath of Sony and Disney failing
to come to an agreement to renegotiate terms

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.640
of its deal that allowed Tom Holland's Spider-Man
to be a part of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.060
Deadpool actor Ryan Reynolds came forward
to address the situation.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.560
Reynolds' response to Spider-Man swinging
out of the MCU was witty as all get-out - which

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:22.340
is to be expected when dealing with the actor
whose tongue is firmly planted in his cheek

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.040
- but it sadly offered fans little comfort
in this tumultuous time.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:31.039
Twitter user @ChaoticKing_ was one of many
fans who turned to Reynolds to help save Spider-Man,

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.920
or at least give them a bit of solace after
having their Spidey-loving hearts shattered.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.700
Clearly hoping for a silver lining in all
the darkness, @ChaoticKing_ asked Reynolds

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:43.620
on Twitter whether Spider-Man's MCU exit could
eventually result in a team-up movie with

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.790
Spider-Man and Deadpool.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.380
Reynolds gave a half-humorous, half-heartbreaking
response:

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.440
"You can.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.520
But you can only see it in my heart."

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.880
If fans weren't sufficiently devastated over
the news that Holland's web-slinging vigilante

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.880
won't be able to play on the Marvel Studios
playground anymore, Reynolds' tweet absolutely

00:00:58.880 --> 00:00:59.840
crushed them.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.260
One fan tweeted at Reynolds,

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.560
"That's literally not the response we wanted.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.700
We wanted a yes.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.140
A big, fat yes.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.400
Please and thank you."

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.040
Another fan begged the actor,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.720
"Ryan pls help us."

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.860
Clearly, sorrowful Spider-Man fans are placing
a lot of stock in Reynolds' ability to either

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.710
roll up his sleeves and duke it out with Sony
executives himself, or do some sort of behind-the-scenes

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.700
string-pulling to get Spider-Man back into
Marvel's movie realm.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.200
"Yeah, it's me, Deadpool, and I got an offer
that you can't refuse!"

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.900
As much as we love Reynolds - and as cool
as it would be to see his raunchy, hard-R-rated

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:36.531
superhero film series collide with Spider-Man's
world - it's strange that so many people are

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.180
wanting him to do something about the Sony-Disney
split.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.060
Granted, Deadpool is a Marvel Comics character
that Marvel Studios hasn't yet been able to

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.670
use in the MCU due to rights restrictions
- which is a fate that Spider-Man had suffered

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.440
up until 2015, when Disney and Sony struck
a deal to let Holland's hero character appear

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.180
in Marvel movies while Sony retained financial,
distribution, and creative control.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.880
But there's a lot more at play here, and there's
basically nothing that Reynolds can do to

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:01.860
change things.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.360
While Reynolds is one of a few actors who
can commiserate with Holland about playing

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:09.719
a Marvel character that isn't allowed in the
MCU, there's a high probability that Reynolds'

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.540
Deadpool actually will join the MCU in the
future.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:18.219
After Disney bought the majority of 20th Century
Fox's assets in a $71.3 billion deal earlier

00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:22.379
this year, the House of Mouse acquired a bunch
of Marvel Comics characters whose screen rights

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.520
resided at Fox.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.499
Deadpool is one of them - and while nothing
has been confirmed by the way of a third Deadpool

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.200
movie or Wade Wilson's forthcoming inclusion
in the MCU, it seems fairly inevitable.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:36.160
The Merc with a Mouth made big money at the
box office and has helped revolutionize the

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.029
superhero genre - sparking studio executives
to consider giving darker, grittier, and more

00:02:41.029 --> 00:02:43.440
violent characters their own franchises.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.960
Plainly put, Disney and Marvel would be fools
not to induct Deadpool into the MCU.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.919
Regardless if that ends up happening, and
even if Reynolds never slips back into the

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.300
red-and-black suit for another Deadpool movie,
Deadpool is property of Marvel Studios.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.560
Spider-Man isn't.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.600
And now that Sony and Disney have done the
corporate equivalent of filing for divorce,

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.160
it's virtually impossible for a Deadpool-Spider-Man
team-up movie to happen.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.920
Reynolds may have a ton of clout in Hollywood
and an unmatched presence on social media,

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.609
but one thing he doesn't have is the power
to squash the beef between two of the biggest

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:14.420
entertainment companies in the world.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.380
Wish as we might that it wasn't so, Peter
Parker and Wade Wilson probably won't ever

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.460
meet.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.760
Like Reynolds, fans will simply have to keep
that dream alive in their hearts.

